[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hello and welcome to Anamotive. Animotive is a VR production tool focused on real-time animation capture for film, TV, games, and previs. It brings performers, creators, and technology together to enable fast,'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'intuitive content production using virtual production and motion capture workflows. Automotive is also built with education in mind, providing a safe space for learning, teaching, and experimenting with real-time animation'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and virtual production techniques. This getting started guide will get you up and running with basics of automotive. First, let\'s review the controls. Controls. An important skill to master is our teleport feature. To teleport'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'around the set, press down and hold the left thumb stick like a button and point your controller at the location on the ground where you\'d like to go. A ring will appear where your hand is pointing.'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A blue ring means you can teleport there. A red ring means you can\'t. When you\'re ready, release the thumb stick to teleport to that location. Try this a'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'few times until you get comfortable. need to turn around. Flick the left thumb stick left or right to snap turn by 30°. We recommend practicing this a few times to get used to the movement.'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Next, you\'ll need to learn how to toggle the menu. To access characters, sets, props, cameras, and lights. Press the B button on your right controller.'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Practice turning the menu on and off to get a feel for it. Select a character. Now it\'s time to select your character.'

[01:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Toggle on your menu by pressing B on your right controller. Point your laser at the left hand menu and highlight assets. Press the right trigger to select it. This opens the character menu. To spawn'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a character, point your laser at the character you want. Press the right trigger once and the character will appear in front of you. Calibration and embodying a character.'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Now you\'re ready to embody your character. Point your right hand laser at the character and press the right trigger. The character will highlight in blue. Look down at your left hand menu and'

[02:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'select embody at the top. You may be prompted to calibrate. If so, press the calibrate button and follow the onscreen steps.'

[02:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This calibration data helps Animotive retarget your motion more accurately to the character. Awesome. You are now embodying the character.'

[02:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'What you\'re seeing is the mirror view, a performance aid that helps you understand your character\'s movement and facial expressions. Take a moment to explore. You can select different hand gestures'

[03:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'by using the thumb sticks and move your character\'s hands into position by pressing the grip buttons. To turn mirror view off, press B to bring up the menu.'

[03:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Select settings, then toggle mirror view off. Press B again to close the menu and begin performing. Start a capture. Ready to start'

[03:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'capturing? Great. While embodying a character, make sure your menu and laser are toggled on using the B button. Teleport to where you want to perform. Once you\'re in position, hold down the Y'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'button on your left controller. A 3second countdown will appear. When the clock runs down, it\'s time to perform. To end the capture, simply tap the Y'

[04:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'button again. Invisible characters. After every capture, you\'ll automatically disembbody your character. Now, it\'s time to spawn an invisible character. These characters act as your'

[04:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'crew, allowing you to move props and cameras while remaining invisible to any cameras in the scene. Toggle on your menu with the B button, then select assets. The invisible character is the first option in the'

[04:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'menu. Select it with the right trigger to spawn it. Just like before, select the character. Look at your left hand menu and choose embody'

[04:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cameras. Now, let\'s spawn your first camera. Toggle on your menu. Select tools and choose camera. Your camera will appear in the scene.'

[04:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To move it, hover over the camera with your laser and hold the grip button. Move your controller to reposition the camera. Push the thumb stick forward or back to'

[05:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'move it closer or farther away. When it\'s in place, release the grip. Let\'s try recording handheld camera movement. Toggle the menu off by pressing B.'

[05:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Reach out with your right hand and grab the base of the camera using the grip. To zoom, keep holding the grip and move the right thumb stick left or right.'

[05:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Practice framing your shot. When you\'re ready, hold down the Y button to start recording. Tap Y again to stop.'

[05:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Lights. No scene is complete without lights. To spawn a spotlight, toggle on your menu, select tools, then choose spotlight.'

[06:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'To place lights and other objects, we use laser grabbing. Animotive has three grabbing modes. Switch between them by holding the grip and flicking the thumb stick left or'

[06:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right. The default is linear mode. Move the light freely by holding the grip and moving your controller. The second mode is parabola mode. Here'

[06:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the light is anchored to the floor and can be moved and rotated through space. The third is quick rotate mode, which allows you to rotate the light simply by'

[06:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rotating your controller. For most lighting setups, use linear mode to position the light, then quick rotate mode to angle it towards your subject. To adjust light settings,'

[07:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'select the light with your laser and press the right trigger. Then use the menu to change angle, color, saturation, and more. coverage. Want more coverage? Try'

[07:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spawning three additional cameras and placing them around your scene. Use the same tools and grab modes you\'ve already learned. Once you\'re happy with your setup, it\'s'

[07:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'time to review your footage. Timeline menu. To review your capture, toggle on your menu and select monitors. Here you can view up to four cameras at'

[08:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'once. Grab the play head and scrub left or right to review your animation in real time. Pretty cool, right? Export. What\'s the point of creating'

[08:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something if you can\'t share it? To export your scene, toggle on your menu and select export. Choose video, select your format, and press export. When the export finishes, a file'

[08:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'explorer window will open with your files. Great job. You\'ve made your first animotive scene. But this is just the beginning. Animotive is packed with'

[08:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'advanced features like text management, prop interaction, motion capture suit integration, camera depth of field, audio workflows, and more. To learn more, check out our support'

[09:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'documentation, YouTube channel, or join our Discord community. We can\'t wait to see what you create.'
